<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Twenty-fifth Dynasty of Egypt</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Twenty-Fifth Dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Twenty-fifth Dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> was a line of Kushite kings from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> who ruled Egypt in the eighth and seventh centuries BCE. Under rulers such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piye">Piye</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taharqa">Taharqa</a> they united the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile-valley">Nile Valley</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napata">Napata</a> to the Delta and revived traditional Egyptian religion and art. They were driven out of Egypt by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyrians</a> but continued to rule Kush, as described in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kushite-empire">Kushite Empire</a> profile.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/twenty-fifth-dynasty-of-egypt.jpg" alt="Twenty-fifth Dynasty of Egypt" width="320" height="261" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthias Gehricke · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rulers_of_Kush,_Kerma_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
